  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Acquires TBPN Business Talk Show\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"OpenAI acquires TBPN, the buzzy founder-led business talk show, showing expansion into media content.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/02/openai-acquires-tbpn-the-buzzy-founder-led-business-talk-show/\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-02\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"acquisition\", \"media\", \"content\", \"m&a\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"Highlights from Lenny's Podcast on Agentic Engineering\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison was a guest on Lenny Rachitsky's podcast discussing 'An AI state of the union: We've passed the inflection point, dark factories are coming, and automation timelines'. Episode covers agentic engineering, coding agents, and the current state of AI development. Available on YouTube, Spotify, and Apple Podcasts.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lennys-podcast/\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-02\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"agentic-engineering\", \"coding-agents\", \"podcast\", \"ai-state-of-union\", \"automation\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"datasette-llm 0.1a6 Released\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Release of datasette-llm 0.1a6, an LLM integration plugin for Datasette that other plugins can depend on. Part of Simon's ongoing work building LLM tooling.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a6\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\", \"llm\", \"plugins\", \"developer-tools\", \"python\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"Agentic-MME: What Agentic Capability Really Brings to Multimodal Intelligence?\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper exploring what agentic capabilities truly bring to multimodal intelligence systems. Investigates the unique advantages of agentic AI architectures in handling complex multimodal tasks.\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"Qianshan Wei et al.\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"agentic-ai\", \"multimodal\", \"research\", \"llm-agents\", \"paper\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"AgentHazard: Benchmark for Evaluating Harmful Behavior in Computer-Use Agents\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper introducing AgentHazard, a benchmark designed to evaluate harmful behaviors in computer-using AI agents. Important for AI safety research as agents gain more autonomy.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"Yunhao Feng et al.\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"ai-safety\", \"agents\", \"benchmark\", \"computer-use\", \"evaluation\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Multi-Turn Reinforcement Learning for Tool-Calling Agents\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper on multi-turn reinforcement learning approaches for tool-calling agents with iterative reward calibration. Addresses challenges in training agents that effectively use external tools.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"Wachiravit Modecrua et al.\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"reinforcement-learning\", \"tool-calling\", \"agents\", \"training\", \"reward-calibration\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"FoE: Forest of Errors Makes First Solution Best in Large Reasoning Models\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper presenting FoE (Forest of Errors), a technique to make the first solution the best in large reasoning models through error-based tree approaches.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"Kehan Jiang et al.\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"reasoning\", \"llm\", \"error-handling\", \"inference\", \"optimization\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   221→  },\n   222→  {\n   223→    \"title\": \"InfoSeeker: Scalable Hierarchical Parallel Agent Framework for Web Information Seeking\",\n   224→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper introducing InfoSeeker, a hierarchical parallel agent framework designed for efficient web information seeking. Addresses scalability in multi-agent web research systems.\",\n   225→    \"author\": \"Ka Yiu Lee et al.\",\n   226→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   227→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   228→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   229→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"web-scraping\", \"hierarchical-agents\", \"information-retrieval\", \"scalability\"],\n   230→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   231→  },\n   232→  {\n   233→    \"title\": \"Automatic Textbook Formalization\",\n   234→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper on automatic formalization of textbooks, using AI to convert educational content into formal mathematical representations. Important for AI education and verification.\",\n   235→    \"author\": \"Fabian Gloeckle et al.\",\n   236→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   237→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   238→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   239→    \"topics\": [\"formalization\", \"education\", \"math\", \"ai\", \"verification\"],\n   240→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   241→  },\n   242→  {\n   243→    \"title\": \"SCRAT: Coupled Control, Structured Memory, and Verifiable Action in Agentic AI\",\n   244→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper presenting SCRAT (Stochastic Control with Retrieval and Auditable Trajectories), drawing insights from squirrel locomotion and scatter-hoarding for agentic AI architectures with verifiable actions.\",\n   245→    \"author\": \"Maximiliano Armesto, Christophe Kolb\",\n   246→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   247→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   248→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   249→    \"topics\": [\"agentic-ai\", \"control\", \"memory\", \"verification\", \"bio-inspired\"],\n   250→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   251→  }\n   252→]\n   253→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
