velopment tools, agents, and the future of software engineering</div>\n            <div class=\"date\">April 7, 2026</div>\n        </header>\n\n        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <section class=\"new-products\">\n                <h2>🆕 New Products</h2>\n                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n                    No new products discovered today. Check back tomorrow for the latest agentic coding tools and platforms.\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2>📋 Whitelist Updates</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases/tag/v1.3.38-vscode\" target=\"_blank\">Continue v1.3.38 for VSCode</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Pre-release builds available for multiple platforms including Alpine Linux, macOS ARM64, and other architectures.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>📅 2026-03-27</span>\n                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback negative\">\n                        <div class=\"quote\">Users experiencing rate limit errors with Claude Sonnet (429 errors) and GPT-5 (400 errors)</div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">Source: GitHub Issues #12057, #12056</div>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"community-feedback positive\">\n                        <div class=\"quote\">Community contributed OpenRouter provider support with dynamic model loading and fuzzy search UI improvements</div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">Source: GitHub PR #8738</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>💡 Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/google-ai-edge-gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Google AI Edge Gallery - Local Gemma 4 Models on iPhone</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google released an official app for running Gemma 4 models directly on iPhone with image Q&A, audio transcription, and tool calling widgets.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">local-llms</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">gemini</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">mobile-ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-ports/releases/tag/0.2\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-ports 0.2 Released</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Tool to find all currently running Datasette instances and list their ports. Now works standalone without Datasette.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">developer-tools</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/openai-alums-have-been-quietly-investing-from-a-new-potentially-100m-fund/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Alums Launch $100M Investment Fund</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        OpenAI alumni have been quietly investing from a new potentially $100M fund, showing continued financial activity in the AI space.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">investment</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">vc</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/google-quietly-releases-an-offline-first-ai-dictation-app-on-ios/\" target=\"_blank\">Google Quietly Launches Offline-First AI Dictation App on iOS</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Google quietly released an AI dictation app that works offline on iOS, similar to the AI Edge Gallery app for running local models.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ios</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">offline-ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/iran-threatens-stargate-ai-data-centers/\" target=\"_blank\">Iran Threatens 'Stargate' AI Data Centers</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Geopolitical tensions involving AI infrastructure as Iran threatens 'Stargate' AI data centers, highlighting strategic importance of AI facilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 6</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-infrastructure</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">geopolitics</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years of Wanting, Three Months of Building with AI</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        AI excels at tedious work but can lead to deferred architectural decisions. Key lesson: AI is great for low-level details but can make you procrastinate on key design decisions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Lalit Maganti)</span>\n                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 5</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/japan-is-proving-experimental-physical-ai-is-ready-for-the-real-world/\" target=\"_blank\">Japan Proving Experimental Physical AI Ready for Real World</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        In Japan, robots aren't coming for jobs - they're filling jobs nobody wants. Shows practical deployment of physical AI in real-world scenarios.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 5</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">physical-ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">robotics</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">japan</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/copilot-is-for-entertainment-purposes-only-according-to-microsofts-terms-of-service/\" target=\"_blank\">Copilot 'For Entertainment Purposes Only' Per Microsoft Terms</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Microsoft's terms of service indicate Copilot is 'for entertainment purposes only', raising questions about liability and production use guarantees for AI coding assistants.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 5</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">microsoft</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">copilot</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">liability</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/kyle-daigle/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Activity Surging: 275 Million Commits Per Week</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        GitHub platform activity is accelerating dramatically. On pace for 14 billion commits this year if growth remains linear. Massive explosion in development activity, likely driven by AI coding tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>Simon Willison (citing Kyle Daigle)</span>\n                        <span class=\"source blog\">Blog</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 4</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">github</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">github-actions</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-activity</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/04/anthropic-says-claude-code-subscribers-will-need-to-pay-extra-for-openclaw-support/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Says Claude Code Subscribers Need Extra Payment for OpenClaw</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic announced that Claude Code subscribers will need to pay extra for OpenClaw usage, introducing new pricing tiers for advanced coding features.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 4</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/openai-executive-shuffle-new-roles-coo-brad-lightcap-fidji-simo-kate-rouch/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Executive Shuffle: New Roles for COO Brad Lightcap</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        OpenAI executive shuffle includes new role for COO Brad Lightcap to lead 'special projects', along with new roles for Fidji Simo and Kate Rouch.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">executives</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">leadership</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/anthropic-buys-biotech-startup-coefficient-bio-in-400m-deal-reports/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Buys Biotech Startup Coefficient Bio in $400M Deal</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Anthropic acquires biotech startup Coefficient Bio in a $400M deal, expanding into AI applications for biotechnology research.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span>TechCrunch</span>\n                        <span class=\"source tech-media\">TechMedia</span>\n                        <span>📅 Apr 3</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">acquisition</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">biotech</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/ai-companies-are-building-huge-natural-gas-plants-to-power-data-centers-what-could-go-wrong/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Companies Building Huge Natural Gas Plants for Data Centers</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        AI companies are constructing massive natural gas power plants to support energy-intensive data centers, raising environmental and infrastructure concerns.\n                 